<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Pippa.app: Hardened Runtime, WITHOUT App Sandbox (a sandboxed app cannot set up and
  start Pi in the user's home folder). Only rights the Hardened Runtime itself requires are listed here.

  - automation.apple-events: the Hardened Runtime otherwise blocks Apple Events (macOS still asks per target app,
    text: NSAppleEventsUsageDescription). Pippa uses it only to read the selected mail and the active sheet in Excel,
    to search Photos (NSAppleScript in its own process, no osascript) and to create unsent drafts in Mail.
  - personal-information.calendars: Hardened Runtime right for EventKit; covers Calendar AND Reminders (there is no
    separate right for Reminders). Without it macOS refuses silently, without a prompt.
  - personal-information.photos-library: Hardened Runtime right for PhotoKit (NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription): previews
    of the photos Pippa's Photos search found. The search itself goes through Apple Events (automation for Photos).
  - personal-information.addressbook: Hardened Runtime right for Contacts (read only, "What Pippa may do").

  Dropped with the sandbox (effective only inside it): app-sandbox, files.user-selected.read-write,
  files.bookmarks.app-scope, files.downloads.read-write, network.client, network.server,
  temporary-exception.apple-events (Mail, Excel), temporary-exception.files.home-relative-path.read-only
  (other apps' model folders) and temporary-exception.mach-lookup.global-name (Sparkle's -spks/-spki).
  Desktop, Documents and Downloads are now protected by TCC (NSDesktop/Documents/DownloadsFolderUsageDescription).

  Deliberately NOT set: cs.disable-library-validation, cs.allow-jit, cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory.
  All dylibs are signed with the same identity at build time; only Node needs JIT (Node.entitlements).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.personal-information.calendars</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.personal-information.photos-library</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.personal-information.addressbook</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
